{"agent":"impact","findings":[{"id":"impact-1","file":"triggarr/web/routes.py","line":45,"title":"Revert of e11187e makes template autoescaping (the XSS protection) depend on a deprecated Starlette kwarg; with unpinned Docker builds this risks a startup outage or lost escaping","category":"blast-radius","cwe":"CWE-79","severity":"high","agent_confidence":70,"in_diff":true,"intent_doc_match":false,"problem":"This diff reverts commit e11187e, whose message says: 'Starlette removed the **env_options passthrough in Jinja2Templates, breaking autoescape=True on newer versions.' Before the diff, an explicitly built jinja2.Environment(autoescape=True) was passed in through env=, so escaping held on any Starlette version. After the diff, the code goes back to Jinja2Templates(directory=..., autoescape=True). That passes autoescape through **env_options, which the installed Starlette 0.52.1 already deprecates. At .venv/.../starlette/templating.py:92-96 it emits 'Extra environment options are deprecated. Use a preconfigured jinja2.Environment instead.' Escaping still works today only because of that deprecated passthrough and the default at templating.py:114 (env_options.setdefault('autoescape', True)). The Dockerfile at line 31 runs `pip install --no-cache-dir .`, which ignores uv.lock, and pyproject lists 'fastapi' with no version bound. So every image build pulls the newest Starlette. Once the kwarg is removed, one of two things happens. Either `autoescape=True` raises TypeError when routes.py is imported, and routes.py is imported by triggarr/__main__.py and triggarr/search/scheduler.py, so the whole daemon fails to start. Or autoescaping becomes whatever the library default is at that point. In the second case, Radarr/Sonarr titles, config values and error strings rendered in the templates are no longer guaranteed to be escaped, which opens the door to script injection.","current_code":"templates = Jinja2Templates(directory=str(TEMPLATES_DIR), autoescape=True)","fix_hint":"Keep the preconfigured jinja2.Environment(loader=FileSystemLoader(TEMPLATES_DIR), autoescape=True) passed via env= (i.e. drop this revert); optionally also pin starlette/fastapi in the Docker build or install from uv.lock.","why_it_matters":"routes.py is imported at startup by __main__.py and scheduler.py, so if the kwarg breaks, the whole service is down: the scheduler daemon and the web UI. If instead escaping lapses silently, the UI renders data that comes from external Radarr/Sonarr instances without escaping it (script injection). The previous commit was made specifically to fix this.","silenced_marker_nearby":false}],"agent_notes":["The diff is an exact revert of e11187e ('fix: use preconfigured jinja2.Environment for autoescape'). It brings back the deprecated Jinja2Templates(**env_options) path that the earlier commit removed on purpose.","Installed Starlette 0.52.1 (uv.lock) still accepts the kwarg but emits a DeprecationWarning (starlette/templating.py:92-96), so behavior is unchanged locally and tests probably still pass. Where the code ends up, the env still has autoescape=True (templating.py:114 setdefault).","Deployment risk: the Dockerfile installs with `pip install .` (line 31), not from uv.lock, and pyproject does not pin fastapi or starlette. A routine image rebuild after Starlette drops env_options would fail at import time. That takes down the whole daemon, not just the web UI, because __main__.py and search/scheduler.py import routes.py.","If pytest is configured to turn warnings into errors (filterwarnings=error), the DeprecationWarning would fail tests/test_web.py and tests/test_middleware.py at import. I found no filterwarnings entry in pyproject.toml.","No public API, schema or performance impact. The only effect is how the module-level `templates` object is built, and its .env is used the same way afterwards (globals['triggarr_version']).","Verdict: blocking. This removes an unconditional autoescape guarantee and replaces it with a deprecated, version-dependent path that the Docker build does not pin. Recommend dropping this change."]}
